        "y1": 0.6804597701149425
      },
      "text": "PESTLE: (1) A leg of an animal, generally of a pig: A pestle of pork is still in common use. Pestels   of venison; P. 98. Pestell of fesshe; jambon; A pestle-pie is a standing pie which con tains a whole gammon, and sometimes a couple at country fairs, and at Christmas fcasts. large",
